{"dossier":"D06","entry_points":[{"sids":["mm/filemap.c::pagecache_init","mm/hugetlb.c::vma_needs_reservation","mm/hugetlb.c::vma_add_reservation","mm/memory.c::zap_pud_range","mm/memory.c::zap_pmd_range","mm/memory.c::__vm_normal_page"],"text":"Boot prepares wait buckets, writeback and VM controls; reservation wrappers translate address for need and add; zap helpers iterate upper and PMD levels; normal resolution gates accountable memory."}],"exports":[{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::alloc_frozen_pages_noprof","mm/mempolicy.c::alloc_pages_noprof","mm/mempolicy.c::folio_alloc_noprof","mm/mempolicy.c::get_task_policy","mm/mempolicy.c::interleave_nid"],"text":"Tiered allocation offers frozen, counted and folio helpers with policy and node resolution, plus task policy lookup and interleave offset mapping."},{"sids":["mm/filemap.c::filemap_invalidate_lock_two","mm/filemap.c::filemap_invalidate_unlock_two","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_bit","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_bit_killable","mm/filemap.c::softleaf_entry_wait_on_locked","mm/filemap.c::folio_end_read","mm/filemap.c::folio_end_private_2","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_private_2","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_private_2_killable"],"text":"Dual invalidation guards up to two mappings, and folio sync provides bit waits, softleaf waits, read completion and private-flag operations."},{"sids":["mm/truncate.c::folio_unmap_invalidate","mm/memory.c::unmap_mapping_folio","mm/memory.c::zap_vma_range_batched","mm/hugetlb.c::__unmap_hugepage_range"],"text":"Teardown invalidates folios, removes single mappings, zaps ranges and unmaps huge ranges with reservation handling."},{"sids":["mm/hugetlb.c::huge_pmd_unshare.alt_1","mm/hugetlb.c::huge_pmd_unshare.alt_2","mm/hugetlb.c::__huge_pmd_unshare.alt_1","mm/hugetlb.c::__huge_pmd_unshare.alt_2","mm/hugetlb.c::huge_pmd_unshare_flush.alt_1","mm/hugetlb.c::huge_pmd_unshare_flush.alt_2","mm/hugetlb.c::hugetlb_mask_last_page.alt_1","mm/hugetlb.c::hugetlb_mask_last_page.alt_2","mm/huge_memory.c::zap_huge_pud","mm/huge_memory.c::__pud_trans_huge_lock","mm/rmap.c::folio_remove_rmap_pud","mm/hugetlb.c::__vma_private_lock","mm/hugetlb.c::hugetlb_vma_assert_locked","mm/hugetlb_cgroup.c::hugetlb_cgroup_uncharge_file_region"],"text":"Huge helpers unshare middle tables with flush, derive spans, zap and lock huge PUD entries, check locks and uncharge regions."},{"sids":["mm/huge_memory.c::deferred_split_folio","mm/rmap.c::folio_remove_rmap_pmd","mm/memory.c::vm_normal_folio_pmd","mm/memory.c::vm_normal_page_pmd","mm/huge_memory.c::zap_huge_pmd","mm/huge_memory.c::__split_huge_pmd","mm/huge_memory.c::split_huge_pmd_locked","mm/huge_memory.c::__pmd_trans_huge_lock","mm/mlock.c::munlock_folio"],"text":"Helpers queue deferred splits, remove PMD rmaps, resolve normal pages, zap, lock and split huge PMDs, and batch munlock."}],"extracts":["1829d07de346f8c9780bdc346abe8892782fd37a2df3fbb32be3359e442d002e","7eee7efaf0e2b99234319a2498aaaa094b11940b10eec355f2c861a631f6e20c","7f9a15ce122f2e3e0a236d256254b71bf472f5b8e8c741454c5b6749bd61c201"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_bit_common","mm/filemap.c::softleaf_entry_wait_on_locked","mm/truncate.c::folio_unmap_invalidate","mm/filemap.c::sysctl_page_lock_unfairness","mm/filemap.c::wake_page_function"],"text":"Lost wakeup is avoided by marking waiters before final check; unfairness budget grants acquisition to avoid starvation; forced removal reports busy on dirty or pinned cases."},{"sids":["mm/hugetlb.c::__unmap_hugepage_range","mm/hugetlb.c::__vma_reservation_common","mm/rmap.c::__folio_remove_rmap","mm/memory.c::print_bad_page_map","mm/huge_memory.c::deferred_split_folio"],"text":"Huge teardown needs huge alignment and exclusive access with clamped intervals; reservation validates modes; rmap races need clamping with deferred reset; out-of-range frames trigger diagnostics; tiny orders skip queuing and device-private avoids splitting."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["mm/mempolicy.c::alloc_pages_preferred_many","mm/hugetlb.c::set_vma_resv_flags","mm/hugetlb.c::is_vma_resv_set","mm/hugetlb.c::vma_resv_map","mm/hugetlb.c::inode_resv_map","mm/hugetlb.c::__vma_reservation_common","mm/hugetlb.c::vma_hugecache_offset"],"text":"Preferred allocation tries the set without reclaim then falls back; private pointer packs map plus flags; shared uses inode map while private decodes it; fault index derives from address; shared presence means reserved while private absence means remaining."},{"sids":["mm/hugetlb.c::region_add","mm/hugetlb.c::region_chg","mm/hugetlb.c::region_abort","mm/hugetlb.c::allocate_file_region_entries","mm/hugetlb.c::add_reservation_in_range","mm/hugetlb.c::hugetlb_resv_map_add","mm/hugetlb.c::coalesce_file_region","mm/hugetlb.c::record_hugetlb_cgroup_uncharge_info","mm/hugetlb.c::copy_hugetlb_cgroup_uncharge_info","mm/hugetlb.c::region_del","mm/memory.c::zap_p4d_range","mm/memory.c::zap_pud_range","mm/huge_memory.c::vma_is_special_huge"],"text":"Probes reserve, commits consume and aborts release; insertion fills gaps and merges on adjacency; splits duplicate refs and full removal uncharges; upper teardown walks boundaries, splits partial huge PUD and zaps whole ones; special huge skips accounting except DAX."},{"sids":["mm/rmap.c::__folio_remove_rmap","mm/memory.c::zap_pmd_range","mm/memory.c::__vm_normal_page","mm/memory.c::pgtable_level_has_pxx_special","mm/huge_memory.c::has_deposited_pgtable","mm/huge_memory.c::zap_huge_pmd_folio","mm/huge_memory.c::normal_or_softleaf_folio_pmd","mm/memory.c::print_bad_page_map","mm/memory.c::__print_bad_page_map_pgtable","mm/huge_memory.c::zap_deposited_table"],"text":"Rmap removal separates small and large folios and levels with clamping; teardown splits partial huge; normal resolution filters special entries; deposited tables follow arch then zero versus device then anon; huge teardown propagates dirty; lookup uses normal or softleaf; diagnostics report corruption."}],"locks":[{"sids":["mm/filemap.c::filemap_invalidate_lock_two","mm/filemap.c::filemap_invalidate_unlock_two","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_bit_common","mm/filemap.c::wake_page_function","mm/filemap.c::folio_trylock_flag","mm/filemap.c::softleaf_entry_wait_on_locked"],"text":"Dual mappings lock in address order with nested higher semantics tolerating nulls; folio waits publish under bucket lock with waiters set before final check, handing softleaf waits from page-table lock to bucket."},{"sids":["mm/truncate.c::folio_unmap_invalidate","mm/memory.c::unmap_mapping_folio","mm/hugetlb.c::__unmap_hugepage_range","mm/memory.c::unmap_mapping_range_tree","mm/huge_memory.c::zap_huge_pud","mm/huge_memory.c::__pud_trans_huge_lock","mm/huge_memory.c::deferred_split_folio","mm/huge_memory.c::zap_huge_pmd","mm/huge_memory.c::__pmd_trans_huge_lock","mm/huge_memory.c::__split_huge_pmd","mm/mlock.c::munlock_folio"],"text":"Detach holds host and cache exclusion; single unmap uses rmap read lock while huge needs write lock with IRQ-serialized restore; PUD keeps lock only for confirmed huge; PMD zap, lock and split hold PMD lock with notifiers; deferred uses read-side plus node lock; munlock batches locally."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F3"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_bit_common","mm/filemap.c::wake_page_function","mm/filemap.c::folio_end_read","mm/filemap.c::folio_end_private_2","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_private_2","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_private_2_killable","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_bit_killable"],"text":"Folio waits try fast acquisition, sleep, requeue on loss and signal done versus woken; wake filters by folio and bit with handoff; read unlocks and validates; private flag clears, wakes and loops with killable abort."},{"sids":["mm/truncate.c::folio_unmap_invalidate","mm/memory.c::zap_vma_range_batched","mm/memory.c::__zap_vma_range","mm/hugetlb.c::__unmap_hugepage_range"],"text":"Invalidation tolerates mapped start then requires clean, stable and releasable to detach else busy; range zap brackets notifiers, delegates huge and walks tables; huge unmap handles absent, shared, empty, special and present slots."},{"sids":["mm/hugetlb.c::__vma_reservation_common","mm/hugetlb.c::vma_needs_reservation","mm/hugetlb.c::vma_add_reservation","mm/huge_memory.c::deferred_split_folio","mm/huge_memory.c::split_huge_pmd_locked"],"text":"Reservation dispatches need, commit, end, add and delete with mirrored shared versus private effects; deferred marks partial once then inserts; split divides huge PMDs with distinct file, migration and device handling."}],"structs":[{"sids":["mm/filemap.c::PAGE_WAIT_TABLE_BITS","mm/filemap.c::PAGE_WAIT_TABLE_SIZE","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_table","mm/filemap.c::pagecache_init","mm/filemap.c::filemap_sysctl_table","mm/filemap.c::sysctl_page_lock_unfairness","mm/filemap.c::behavior","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_bit_common","mm/filemap.c::folio_wait_bit"],"text":"Waits share 256 buckets from eight bits initialized at boot with exclusive, shared and dropping intents; fairness tunable page_lock_unfairness defaults to five, floor zero, mode 0644."}],"stubs":[{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock.h::spin_lock_irq","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock.h::spin_unlock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock.h::spin_unlock_irq","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock_rt.h::spin_lock_irq","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock_rt.h::spin_unlock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/linux/spinlock_rt.h::spin_unlock_irq","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_load_acquire.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D03"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_load_acquire.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier"